{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>By the cubit of a man.</b> By the cubit of each one of those Rephaim. The word אִישׁ denotes each and every individual, as in אִישׁ לְבִצְעוֹ מִקָּצֵהוּ (Isaiah 56:11), וַיַּכּוּ אִישׁ אִישׁוֹ (I Kings 20:20), and others. That is to say: even though that bed was nine cubits long by the cubit of each one of them, it was without doubt very many more than nine ordinary cubits — perhaps several times over. From this one grasps the great size and strength of those giants. And despite all this, the children of Ammon annihilated them by the decree of the blessed El, as explained above (Deuteronomy 2:21)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:20:18.869777521Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}